{{also|keks}}
==German==

===Etymology===
{{bor|en|cakes|lang=de}}, 1900s. Popularized by German food company {{w|Bahlsen}} which changed the brand name of their biscuits from ''Leibniz-Cakes'' to ''Leibniz-Keks'' in 1911; at the time, the plural was also {{m|de|Keks}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/keːks/|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m|g2=n|Kekses|Kekse}}

# [[cookie]] {{qualifier|US}}, [[biscuit]] {{qualifier|UK}}

====Usage notes====
The word is always masculine in northern and central Germany. In the southern half of the language area it is often neuter.

====Related terms====
* {{l|de|Keksdose}}
* {{l|de|auf den Keks gehen}}

